WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.932
A subquery in FROM is called a derived table The
inner query produces

00:00:05.959 --> 00:00:11.688
rows and columns The outer query treats those rows
like an intermediate

00:00:11.715 --> 00:00:17.442
table for that statement This is especially useful
when you want to aggregate

00:00:17.468 --> 00:00:23.737
first and then join Always ask what one row in the
derived table represents
